Chapter: ChessLegality
  cites Games chapter Chess

 Square indices used below: a8 = 0, b8 = 1, c7 = 10, e8 = 4, e2 = 52,
 e1 = 60, a1 = 56, b1 = 57.

 Perft 4 from the start position is 197281, and unlike depths 1 to 3 that
 number counts LEGAL moves: a check first arises at ply 3 (1.e4 d5 2.Bb5+),
 so a pseudo-legal generator cannot reach it. Depths 1 to 3 are repeated here
 as the control that the filter removed nothing it should have kept.

 We say:

Section: Scenario Boards

  three-piece : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> ChessBoard
  three-piece (sa) (pa) (sb) (pb) (sc) (pc) (side) =
    let b1 = chess-place chess-blank sa pa
    in let b2 = chess-place b1 sb pb
    in let b3 = chess-place b2 sc pc
    in chess-to-move b3 side

  four-piece : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> ChessBoard
  four-piece (sa) (pa) (sb) (pb) (sc) (pc) (sd) (pd) (side) =
    let b1 = chess-place chess-blank sa pa
    in let b2 = chess-place b1 sb pb
    in let b3 = chess-place b2 sc pc
    in let b4 = chess-place b3 sd pd
    in chess-to-move b4 side

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

Section: A Pinned Piece Has No Legal Move

 The white bishop on e2 stands between its own king on e1 and a black rook on
 e8. Every square the bishop can reach leaves the king on the open file, so
 the pseudo-legal count and the legal count must disagree, and the king's own
 four squares are what remains.

  pin-lines : [Console] Nothing
  pin-lines =
    let b = three-piece 60 6 52 3 4 10 0
    in let pseudo = chess-moves b
    in let legal = chess-legal b
    in act
      print-line-uni ("pinned bishop pseudo " & show (chess-count-from pseudo 52))
      print-line-uni ("pinned bishop legal " & show (chess-count-from legal 52))
      print-line-uni ("king pseudo " & show (chess-count-from pseudo 60))
      print-line-uni ("king legal " & show (chess-count-from legal 60))
      print-line-uni ("all pseudo " & show (list-length pseudo))
      print-line-uni ("all legal " & show (list-length legal))
      print-line-uni ("white in check " & yn (chess-in-check b 0))
      print-line-uni ("white king found at " & show (chess-king-sq b 0))
    end

Section: Mate, Near Mate, And Stalemate

 The mate is the back rank: the black king on a8 is checked along the a file
 and every square it can reach is covered by the second rook. Removing that
 rook is the near mate, and it must leave exactly two squares. The stalemate
 shares the shape and differs in one respect, that the king is NOT attacked,
 which is the distinction the two predicates exist to make.

  end-lines : [Console] Nothing
  end-lines =
    let mate = four-piece 0 12 56 4 57 4 60 6 1
    in let near = three-piece 0 12 56 4 60 6 1
    in let stale = three-piece 0 12 10 5 60 6 1
    in act
      print-line-uni ("mate: in check " & yn (chess-in-check mate 1) & " legal " & show (list-length (chess-legal mate)) & " checkmate " & yn (chess-checkmate mate) & " stalemate " & yn (chess-stalemate mate))
      print-line-uni ("near: in check " & yn (chess-in-check near 1) & " legal " & show (list-length (chess-legal near)) & " checkmate " & yn (chess-checkmate near) & " stalemate " & yn (chess-stalemate near))
      print-line-uni ("stale: in check " & yn (chess-in-check stale 1) & " legal " & show (list-length (chess-legal stale)) & " checkmate " & yn (chess-checkmate stale) & " stalemate " & yn (chess-stalemate stale))
      print-line-uni ("start: in check " & yn (chess-in-check chess-new 0) & " checkmate " & yn (chess-checkmate chess-new) & " stalemate " & yn (chess-stalemate chess-new))
    end

Section: Perft With The Filter

  perft-lines : [Console] Nothing
  perft-lines =
    let start = chess-new
    in let p1 = chess-perft start 1
    in let p2 = chess-perft start 2
    in let p3 = chess-perft start 3
    in let p4 = chess-perft start 4
    in act
      print-line-uni ("legal perft 1 " & show (p1))
      print-line-uni ("legal perft 2 " & show (p2))
      print-line-uni ("legal perft 3 " & show (p3))
      print-line-uni ("legal perft 4 " & show (p4))
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    pin-lines
    end-lines
    perft-lines
  end

